{"name":"Dragon Ball","hex":"#ff9922","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dragon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical reptilian or serpentine creature.","In European mythologies, a gigantic beast, typically reptilian with leathery bat-like wings, lion-like claws, scaly skin and a lizard-like body, often a monster with fiery breath."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of drag queen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragon"},{"term":"ball","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A solid or hollow sphere, or roughly spherical mass.","A quantity of string, thread, etc., wound into a spherical shape."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form or wind into a ball.","To heat in a furnace and form into balls for rolling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ball"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dragon Ball","blocks":[{"text":"Dragon Ball  is a Japanese media franchise created by Akira Toriyama. The series follows the adventures of protagonist Son Goku from his childhood through adulthood as he trains in martial arts. Along his journey, he makes several friends, becomes a family man, discovers his alien heritage, and battles a wide variety of villains, many of whom, like him, seek the mystical orbs called the Dragon Balls in order to summon a wish-granting dragon."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_Ball"},{"title":"Dragon Ball (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Dragon Ball  is a Japanese anime television series produced by Toei Animation. It ran for a total of 153 episodes on Fuji Television and its FNS affiliates from February 26, 1986, to April 19, 1989. The series adapts the first 194 chapters of the manga series Dragon Ball by Akira Toriyama, which was published in Weekly Shōnen Jump from 1984 to 1995. The anime was broadcast in 81 countries worldwide and is the first animated television series in the Dragon Ball franchise. It follows the adventures of Goku, a young eccentric boy with a monkey tail and exceptional strength who has a passion for fighting and battling enemies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Dragon_Ball_anime_logo.png/330px-Dragon_Ball_anime_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_Ball_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Dragon","blocks":[{"text":"A dragon is a mythical creature found in the folklore of cultures throughout the world. It is roughly serpentine in form, and often possesses features drawn from different animals, such as wings and claws. In nearly all cultures, it is conceived of as a powerful and awe-inspiring creature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png/330px-St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon"},{"title":"Ball","blocks":[{"text":"A ball is a round object. Balls can have several uses. For example they are used in ball games, where the play of the game follows the state of the ball as it is hit, kicked or thrown by players. Balls can also be used for simpler activities, such as catch or juggling. Balls made from hard-wearing materials are used in engineering applications to provide very low friction bearings, known as ball bearings. Black-powder weapons use stone and metal balls as projectiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Many_balls.jpg/330px-Many_balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/05/Wiki_DragonBall_Earth.png/500px-Wiki_DragonBall_Earth.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/05/Wiki_DragonBall_Earth.png/500px-Wiki_DragonBall_Earth.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Earth of Dragon Ball, as published in Daizenshuu 4: World Guide","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWiki_DragonBall_Earth.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/24/Weekly_Sh%C5%8Dnen_Jump_No._51_%28Dec._1984%29_is_the_first_appearance_of_Goku._Cover_art_by_Akira_Toriyama.jpg/250px-Weekly_Sh%C5%8Dnen_Jump_No._51_%28Dec._1984%29_is_the_first_appearance_of_Goku._Cover_art_by_Akira_Toriyama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/24/Weekly_Sh%C5%8Dnen_Jump_No._51_%28Dec._1984%29_is_the_first_appearance_of_Goku._Cover_art_by_Akira_Toriyama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/24/Weekly_Sh%C5%8Dnen_Jump_No._51_%28Dec._1984%29_is_the_first_appearance_of_Goku._Cover_art_by_Akira_Toriyama.jpg/250px-Weekly_Sh%C5%8Dnen_Jump_No._51_%28Dec._1984%29_is_the_first_appearance_of_Goku._Cover_art_by_Akira_Toriyama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The first Dragon Ball chapter debuted in Weekly Shōnen Jump No. 51, December 3, 1984.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWeekly_Sh%C5%8Dnen_Jump_No._51_(Dec._1984)_is_the_first_appearance_of_Goku._Cover_art_by_Akira_Toriyama.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ea/Dragon_Ball_Z_arcade_conversion_kit_by_Banpresto.jpg/330px-Dragon_Ball_Z_arcade_conversion_kit_by_Banpresto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ea/Dragon_Ball_Z_arcade_conversion_kit_by_Banpresto.jpg/330px-D